Both files compile cleanly. Here's a summary of everything delivered:

### `app/auth.py`
- `require_api_key` now checks `x_api_key` against `VALID_API_KEYS`
- Raises `HTTP 401` when the header is missing or the key is unrecognized
- Returns the associated username on success

### `app/main.py`

| Endpoint | Change |
|----------|--------|
| `GET /tasks` | Added optional `status`, `priority`, `assigned_to` filters (all combinable). Added `page` (default 1) and `page_size` (default 20, max 100) pagination. |
| `POST /tasks` | New. Requires auth. Validates `project_id` exists (404 if not). Auto-generates sequential integer ID. Returns 201 with the created task. |
| `PUT /tasks/{task_id}` | New. Requires auth. Partial update via `exclude_unset=True` — only provided fields are applied. Returns 404 if task not found. |
| `DELETE /tasks/{task_id}` | New. Requires auth. Removes the task and returns 204. Returns 404 if not found. |

All endpoints follow the existing patterns — same list iteration style as `get_task`, same `HTTPException` usage, Pydantic v2 `model_dump()` throughout.
